	('2026-03-24 08:18:45.374493+00', '{ARC,outcome,"INTERVENTIONS: Record interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_ivfluid_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of parenteral or intravenous (IV) fluid is prescribed as a replacement of fluid, electrolytes, calories, vitamins, and other nutritional substances. Crystalloid fluids refers to solutions of mineral salts, including normal (0.9%) saline, Lactated Ringer''s/Hartman''s solution, 5% dextrose in water, 10% dextrose in water, hypotonic and hypertonic saline, among others. Albumin refers to intravenous preparations of purified human serum albumin used to replace lost albumin in patients with hypoalbuminemia, to treat hypovolemia and ascites, and as a part of some diagnostic imaging kits. Common albumin colloid solutions include Albumin 4%, 5% and 20% among others. Gelatin refers to a colloidal, isotonic, physiologically balanced, plasma volume substitute containing succinylated gelatine and electrolytes, with potential nephroprotective properties. Common gelatin parenteral fluids include Gelaspan, Gelofusine, Geloplasma, Isoplex, among others. Starches refers to an intravenous solution of hydroxyethyl starch (HES), synthetic, nonionic hydroxyethyl derivative of starch used as a plasma expander when prepared in an isotonic solution. Common starch based, synthetic colloid, parenteral fluids include hydroxyethyl starch (HES) products, among others.', NULL, 99186),
	('2026-03-24 08:18:45.374493+00', '{ARC,outcome,"INTERVENTIONS: Record interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_ivfluid_type}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) corresponding to the parenteral fluid(s) administered.', NULL, 99187),
