	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,lesion_headt}', 'question', 'If yes: Type of head, face or neck lesions', '{Vesicle,Pustule,"Ulcerated lesions","Necrotising lesions","Fungating lesions","Haemorrhagic lesions",Other}', 100784),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,lesion_headt}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the head, face or neck. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface. ', NULL, 100785),
