	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,diagn_bacte}', 'question', 'Bacterial infection', '{"Lab confirmed","Lab negative","Not tested",Unknown}', 101723),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,diagn_bacte}', 'definition', 'Refers to the method of identifying or excluding a bacterial infection in this admission.', NULL, 101724),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,diagn_bacte}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the single most appropriate option that represents the method of identifying or excluding a bacterial infection in this admission.', NULL, 101725),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,diagn_pathounlist}', 'question', 'Other pathogen(s) detected', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101726),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,diagn_pathounlist}', 'definition', 'This refers to the detection of other pathogens, not listed above.', NULL, 101727),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,diagn_pathounlist}', 'completionGuide', 'Specify other detected pathogens, not listed above.', NULL, 101728),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,diagn_clinpneumonia}', 'question', 'Clinical pneumonia diagnosed?', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101729),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,diagn_clinpneumonia}', 'definition', 'Pneumonia refers to infection of the lung often accompanied by inflammation.', NULL, 101730),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,diagn_clinpneumonia}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'' if pneumonia was clinically diagnosed at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101731),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_strokecva}', 'question', 'Stroke / cerebrovascular accident', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101732),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_strokecva}', 'definition', 'Defined as a sudden loss of neurological function secondary to haemorrhage or ischemia in the brain parenchyma due to a vascular event. Stroke may be a clinical diagnosis, with or without supportive radiological findings.', NULL, 101733),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_strokecva}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101734),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severeneuro}', 'question', 'Severe neurological disease', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101735),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severeneuro}', 'definition', 'This refers to various neurological manifestations including meningitis, encephalitis, encephalopathy, acute symptomatic seizures, intracranial haemorrhage or stroke, and Guillain-Barre syndrome (GBS). Meningitis is an inflammatory disease of the leptomeninges, the tissues surrounding the brain and spinal cord, and is defined by an abnormal number of white blood cells in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) within an appropriate clinical context and with or without supportive radiological findings. Encephalitis refers to inflammation of the brain. In comparison with meningitis, in encephalitis, abnormalities in brain function are expected, including altered mental status, motor or sensory deficits, altered behaviour and personality changes, and speech or movement disorders. It is defined by an altered mental status lasting ?24 hours along with two of the following criteria: documented fever >/= 38°C (100.4°F); white blood cell count (WBC) in cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) >/= 5  cells/mm^3; generalized or partial seizures not fully attributable to a preexisting seizure disorder; new onset of focal neurological findings; presence of compatible acute lesion on neuroimaging; abnormality on electroencephalography that is consistent with encephalitis and not attributable to another cause. As outlined by the 2013 International Encephalitis Consortium. Seizures are defined as an intermittent abnormality of nervous system physiology characterised by a transient occurrence of sudden, violent, irregular movement of the body, caused by involuntary contraction of muscles due to abnormal excessive or synchronous neuronal activity in the brain. An established history of epilepsy is not required. Stroke refers to a sudden loss of neurological function secondary to haemorrhage or ischemia in the brain parenchyma due to a vascular event. Stroke may be a clinical diagnosis, with or without supportive radiological findings. Intracranial haemorrhage refers to haemorrhage/bleeding occurring within the skull. Intracranial haemorrhage encompasses four broad types of haemorrhage: epidural haemorrhage, subdural haemorrhage, subarachnoid haemorrhage, and intraparenchymal haemorrhage. Guillain-Barre syndrome refers to a rapidly progressive autoimmune disorder of the peripheral nervous system characterized by limb paraesthesia, areflexia, and generalized muscle weakness or paralysis that often begins in the legs and spreads to the arms, torso, and face. Required features include progressive weakness of the arms and/or legs, ranging from minimal weakness of the legs to total paralysis of all four limbs, and including the trunk, bulbar and facial muscles, and external ophthalmoplegia; and areflexia or decreased deep tendon reflexes in weak limbs. Supportive features include symptom progression over days to four weeks; Relatively symmetric, bilateral symptoms; Pain in the trunk or limbs; Cranial nerve symptoms or signs; Autonomic dysfunction; Sensory dysfunction that is mild; No fever at symptom onset; CSF with elevated protein and normal to mildly elevated leukocyte count (usually <5 cells/mm3); Electrodiagnostic abnormalities consistent with GBS; Recovery starting two to four weeks after progression halts.', NULL, 101736),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severeneuro}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101737),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_seizure}', 'question', 'Seizure', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101738),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_seizure}', 'definition', 'Defined as an intermittent abnormality of nervous system physiology characterised by a transient occurrence of sudden, violent, irregular movement of the body, caused by involuntary contraction of muscles due to abnormal excessive or synchronous neuronal activity in the brain. An established history of epilepsy is not required.', NULL, 101739),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_seizure}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101740),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_focalneuro}', 'question', 'Focal neurological signs', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101741),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_uti}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101854),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_focalneuro}', 'definition', 'Defined as as impairments of nerve, spinal cord, or brain function that affect a specific region of the body, e.g. weakness in the left arm, the right leg, paresis, or plegia, identified in neurological examination.', NULL, 101742),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_focalneuro}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101743),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_encephalitis}', 'question', 'Encephalitis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101744),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_encephalitis}', 'definition', 'Encephalitis refers to inflammation of the brain. It is defined by an altered mental status lasting greater or equal to 24 hours along with two of the following criteria: documented fever greater or equal to 38° C (100.4°F); white blood cell count (WBC) in cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) greater or equal to 5/mm³; generalized or partial seizures not fully attributable to a preexisting seizure disorder; new onset of focal neurological findings; presence of compatible acute lesion on neuroimaging; abnormality on electroencephalography that is consistent with encephalitis and not attributable to another cause. As outlined by the 2013 International Encephalitis Consortium.', NULL, 101745),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_encephalitis}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101746),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_meningitis}', 'question', 'Meningitis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101747),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_meningitis}', 'definition', 'Meningitis is defined by an abnormal number of white blood cells in the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) within an appropriate clinical context and with or without supportive radiological findings.', NULL, 101748),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_meningitis}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101749),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_myocardial}', 'question', 'Myocardial infarction', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101750),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_myocardial}', 'definition', 'Defined as myocardial ischaemia leading to injury/necrosis, diagnosed by clinical findings, altered electrocardiography and elevated cardiac enzymes.', NULL, 101751),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_myocardial}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101752),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiacisc}', 'question', 'Cardiac ischaemia', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101753),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiacisc}', 'definition', 'Defined as diminished blood and oxygen supply to the heart muscle as indicated by typical symptomatology (e.g. chest pain) and confirmed by an electrocardiogram (showing ischaemic changes, e.g. ST depression or elevation) and/or cardiac enzyme elevation (e.g. raised troponin I).', NULL, 101754),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiacisc}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101755),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_endocardit}', 'question', 'Endocarditis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101756),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_endocardit}', 'definition', 'This refers to an inflammation of the endocardium (inner lining of the heart). It is often caused by a primary disorder or microorganisms including bacteria, viruses, fungi, and rickettsiae Diagnosis of infective endocarditis is according to modified Duke criteria, using evidence from microbiological results, echocardiogram and clinical signs.', NULL, 101757),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_endocardit}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101758),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiomyop}', 'question', 'Cardiomyopathy', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101759),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiomyop}', 'definition', 'This refers to structural and functional disorders of myocardium commonly diagnosed by echocardiography. Cardiomyopathy can be primary (genetic) or secondary (e.g. following myocardial infarction).', NULL, 101760),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiomyop}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101761),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_chf}', 'question', 'Congestive heart failure', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101762),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_chf}', 'definition', 'Defined as failure of the heart to pump a sufficient amount of blood to meet the needs of the body tissues, resulting in tissue congestion and oedema. Signs and symptoms include shortness of breath, pitting oedema, enlarged tender liver, engorged neck veins, and pulmonary rales. There are many ways to assess cardiac function (e.g. echocardiography, right heart catheterization, functional testing and supportive biochemical tests). However, there is no diagnostic test for heart failure, since it is largely a clinical diagnosis that is based upon a careful history and physical examination.', NULL, 101763),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_chf}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101764),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiarrhy}', 'question', 'Cardiac arrhythmia', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101765),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiarrhy}', 'definition', 'Refers to any variation from the normal rate or rhythm (which may include the origin of the impulse and/or its subsequent propagation) in the heart, confirmed by electrocardiographic monitoring.', NULL, 101766),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiarrhy}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101767),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiarrest}', 'question', 'Cardiac arrest', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101768),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiarrest}', 'definition', 'Cardiopulmonary arrest or circulatory arrest is defined as the sudden cessation of cardiac activity in an individual who becomes unresponsive, without normal breathing and no signs of circulation.', NULL, 101769),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cardiarrest}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101770),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_myocarditis}', 'question', 'Myocarditis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101771),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_rhabdomyol}', 'question', 'Rhabdomyolysis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101855),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_myocarditis}', 'definition', 'This refers to inflammation of the muscle tissue of the heart (myocarditis) / an inflammatory process affecting the pericardium (pericarditis). It may be diagnosed clinically, with assistance from an echocardiogram, EKG, laboratory or radiological tests.', NULL, 101772),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_myocarditis}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101773),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pericarditis}', 'question', 'Pericarditis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101774),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pericarditis}', 'definition', 'This refers to inflammation of the muscle tissue of the heart (myocarditis) / an inflammatory process affecting the pericardium (pericarditis). It may be diagnosed clinically, with assistance from an echocardiogram, EKG, laboratory or radiological tests.', NULL, 101775),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pericarditis}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101776),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_viralpneum}', 'question', 'Viral pneumonia / pneumonitis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101777),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_viralpneum}', 'definition', 'Defined as pneumonitis (pneumonia) that is believed to occur as a direct consequence of an infecting virus/infecting viruses. Viral pneumonitis may be a clinical diagnosis, with or without radiographic or histopathological evidence of lung consolidation. Although preferred, identification of the infecting viral species is not essential to make the diagnosis.', NULL, 101778),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_viralpneum}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101779),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_bacpneumo}', 'question', 'Bacterial pneumonia', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101780),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_bacpneumo}', 'definition', 'Defined as pneumonia (pneumonitis) that is believed to occur as a direct consequence of infecting bacteria. It is an acute infection of the lung parenchyma caused by bacteria (e.g., Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae, Chlamydia pneumoniae, Mycoplasma pneumoniae, and Legionella pneumophila). Signs and symptoms include productive cough, fever, chills, shortness of breath, and chest pain. Bacterial pneumonia may be a clinical diagnosis, with or without radiographic or histopathological evidence of lung consolidation. Although preferred, identification of the infecting bacterial species is not essential to make the diagnosis.', NULL, 101781),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_bacpneumo}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101782),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pneumothor}', 'question', 'Pneumothorax', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101783),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pneumothor}', 'definition', 'Defined as the abnormal presence of air in the pleural cavity (between the lungs and the chest wall), causing collapse of the lung. It may be diagnosed clinically, usually with radiological confirmation.', NULL, 101784),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pneumothor}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101785),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pleuraleff}', 'question', 'Pleural effusion', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101786),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pleuraleff}', 'definition', 'Defined as increased amounts of fluid within the pleural cavity. Symptoms include shortness of breath, cough, and chest pain. It is usually caused by lung infections, congestive heart failure, pleural and lung tumours, connective tissue disorders, and trauma. It may be diagnosed clinically, with or without radiological or interventional confirmation.', NULL, 101787),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pleuraleff}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101788),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_copneumoni}', 'question', 'Cryptogenic organising pneumonia (COP)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101789),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_copneumoni}', 'definition', 'This refers to an idiopathic diffuse interstitial lung disease, diagnosed radiologically (multiple consolidative or ground glass opacities) or histologically (granulation tissue and chronic inflammatory infiltrate in alveoli). Formerly known as bronchiolitis obliterans organizing pneumonia (BOOP).', NULL, 101790),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_copneumoni}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101791),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_bronchioli}', 'question', 'Bronchiolitis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101792),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_bronchioli}', 'definition', 'This refers to Inflammation of the bronchioles. In adults, bronchiolitis is a general term used to describe a nonspecific Inflammation of the bronchioles characterized by swelling of the bronchioles and mucus accumulation. It is usually caused by the respiratory syncytial virus and affects children. Signs and symptoms include coughing, wheezing, and shortness of breath. In the majority of cases, open or thoracoscopic lung biopsy is required to make a definitive diagnosis, although tissue confirmation may not be necessary in patients with a clear predisposition and typical radiological findings. In infants and children, bronchiolitis is defined as an illness in children <2 years of age, characterized by wheezing and airway obstruction due to primary infection or reinfection with a viral or bacterial pathogen, resulting in inflammation of the small airways/bronchioles. This is a clinical diagnosis, generally in children < 2 years old.', NULL, 101793),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_bronchioli}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101794),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_ards}', 'question', 'Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (ARDS)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101795),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_pe}', 'definition', 'Defined as the occlusion of a pulmonary artery by thrombus, air or fat. Physician diagnosis based on clinical signs and/or radiological tests (e.g. computed tomographic pulmonary angiography and/or ventilation/perfusion scanning).', NULL, 101823),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_pe}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101824),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_dvt}', 'question', 'If yes to thromboembolism: Deep vein thrombosis (DVT)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101825),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_ards}', 'definition', 'Acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) has been defined by the 2012 Berlin criteria:
1. Respiratory symptoms must have begun within one week of a known clinical insult, or the patient must have new or worsening symptoms during the past week.
2. Bilateral opacities consistent with pulmonary oedema must be present on a chest radiograph or computed tomographic (CT) scan. These opacities must not be fully explained by pleural effusions, lobar collapse, lung collapse, or pulmonary nodules.
3. The patient''s respiratory failure must not be fully explained by cardiac failure or fluid overload. An objective assessment (eg, echocardiography) to exclude hydrostatic pulmonary oedema is required if no risk factors for ARDS are present.
4. A moderate to severe impairment of oxygenation must be present, as defined by the ratio of arterial oxygen tension to fraction of inspired oxygen (PaO2/FiO2). The severity of the hypoxaemia defines the severity of the ARDS:
	- Mild ARDS: The PaO2/FiO2 is >200 mmHg, but less than (or equal to) 300 mmHg, on ventilator settings that include positive end-expiratory pressure (PEEP) or continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP) greater than (or equal to) 5 cm H2O.
	- Moderate ARDS: The PaO2/FiO2 is >100 mmHg, but less than (or equal to) 200 mmHg, on ventilator settings that include PEEP ?5 cm H2O.
	- Severe ARDS: The PaO2/FiO2 is less than (or equal to) 100 mmHg on ventilator settings that include PEEP greater than (or equal to) 5 cm H2O.', NULL, 101796),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_ards}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101797),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_ascite}', 'question', 'Ascites', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101798),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_ascite}', 'definition', 'This refers to pathological increase in amount of fluid in the abdominal cavity (ascites). It may be diagnosed clinically, with or without radiological or interventional confirmation. Symptoms associated with ascites include increasing abdominal girth, abdominal discomfort and distension, shortness of breath.', NULL, 101799),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_ascite}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101800),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pancreatit}', 'question', 'Pancreatitis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101801),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pancreatit}', 'definition', 'This refers to acute inflammation of the pancreas. Acute pancreatitis is diagnosed clinically with supporting biochemical (e.g serum amylase or serum lipase) and/or radiological and/or histological evidence. All evidence should be considered together, since no single feature is diagnostic of acute pancreatitis.', NULL, 101802),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_pancreatit}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101803),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_acutehepat}', 'question', 'Acute hepatitis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101804),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_acutehepat}', 'definition', 'This refers to acute hepatic injury resulting from inflammation accompanied by increased serum alanine transaminase (ALT) activity. Etiologies include viral hepatitis, drugs, toxins, and autoimmune disorders.', NULL, 101805),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_acutehepat}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101806),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severeliver}', 'question', 'Severe liver disease (new onset)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101807),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severeliver}', 'definition', 'Defined as cirrhosis and portal hypertension with variceal bleeding, ascites, jaundice or status post liver transplantation.', NULL, 101808),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severeliver}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101809),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_hepaticenc}', 'question', 'If yes to severe liver disease (new onset): Hepatic encephalopathy (any grade)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101810),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_hepaticenc}', 'definition', 'This refers to a constellation of signs and symptoms characterized by changes in personality, consciousness, and reflexes, resulting from neuropsychiatric abnormalities secondary to liver failure and/or portal-systemic blood shunting without evidence of other brain disease. Clinical features include lethargy; confusion (can progress to coma); asterixis; pathologic nystagmus; brisk oculovestibular reflexes; decorticate and decerebrate posturing; muscle spasticity; and bilateral extensor plantar reflexes.', NULL, 101811),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_hepaticenc}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101812),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_jaundice}', 'question', 'If yes to severe liver disease (new onset): Jaundice', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101813),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_jaundice}', 'definition', 'This refers to a clinical manifestation of hyperbilirubinemia, characterized by the yellowish staining of the skin, mucous membrane and/or sclera. ', NULL, 101814),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_jaundice}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101815),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_liverdysfu}', 'question', 'Liver dysfunction', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101816),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_liverdysfu}', 'definition', 'This refers to a finding that indicates abnormal liver function, may refer to any of the following: Clinical jaundice; Hyperbilirubinemia (blood bilirubin level twice the upper limit of the normal range); An increase in alanine transaminase (ALT) or aspartate transaminase (AST) that is twice the upper limit of the normal range.', NULL, 101817),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_liverdysfu}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101818),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_yn}', 'question', 'Thromboembolism', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101819),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_yn}', 'definition', 'Defined as the occlusion of the lumen of a blood vessel by a thrombus that has migrated from a distal site via the blood stream.', NULL, 101820),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_yn}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101821),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_pe}', 'question', 'If yes to thromboembolism: Pulmonary embolism (PE)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101822),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_dvt}', 'definition', 'Defined as the presence of a blood clot in a deep vein, predominantly in the lower extremity, but may include the pelvis or upper extremity. Symptoms may include pain, swelling, warmth, and redness in the affected area. Physician diagnosis based on clinical signs and/or appropriate diagnostic imaging e.g. ultrasonography.', NULL, 101826),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_dvt}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101827),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_oth}', 'question', 'If yes to thromboembolism: Other thromboembolism (not PE or DVT)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101828),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to thromboembolic diagnoses not specified above.', NULL, 101829),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_oth}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101830),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_spec}', 'question', 'If yes: Specify other thromboembolism', NULL, 101831),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_spec}', 'definition', 'This refers to the other thromboembolic diagnoses not specified above.', NULL, 101832),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_thrombemb_spec}', 'completionGuide', 'If ''Other'', write the other thromboembolic diagnoses the patient experienced at any time during hospitalisation. ', NULL, 101833),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_anaemia}', 'question', 'Anaemia', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101834),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_anaemia}', 'definition', 'Defined as a reduction in the number of red blood cells, the amount of haemoglobin, and/or the volume of packed red blood cells. Clinically, anaemia represents a reduction in the oxygen-transporting capacity of a designated volume of blood, resulting from an imbalance between blood loss (through haemorrhage or haemolysis) and blood production. Signs and symptoms of anaemia may include pallor of the skin and mucous membranes, shortness of breath, palpitations of the heart, soft systolic murmurs, lethargy, and fatigability. The World Health Organization thresholds are used for defining anaemia, for example in adult males aged over 15 years anaemia is defined by a haemoglobin <130g/L (<8.1mmol/L); for non-pregnant females aged over 15 years thresholds are <120g/L (<7.4mmol/L).', NULL, 101835),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_anaemia}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101836),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severebleed_yn}', 'question', 'Severe bleeding (requiring intervention)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101837),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severebleed_yn}', 'definition', 'Defined as bleeding resulting in haemodynamic compromise necessitating intervention, namely transfusion. This includes World Health Organisation (WHO) Bleeding Scale grade 3 or 4.', NULL, 101838),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severebleed_yn}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101839),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severebleed_site}', 'question', 'If yes: Severe bleeding site(s)', '{Skin,Petechiae,Nose,Gums,"GI tract","Urinary tract",Vagina,Other(s),Unknown}', 101840),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severebleed_site}', 'definition', 'This refers to the location of bleeding/haemorrhage site(s). Petechiae refer to small reddish or purplish spots in skin or mucous membrane as a result of localised haemorrhage. Nose bleeding refers to haemorrhage localized in the nose. Gum bleeding refers to haemorrhage affecting the gingiva. Gastrointestinal (GI) bleeding refers to haemorrhage in any segment of the gastrointestinal tract from oesophagus to rectum. Urinary tract bleeding refers to haemorrhage originating from any part of the urinary system. Vaginal bleeding refers to haemorrhage originating from vagina, unrelated to normal menstruation.', NULL, 101841),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severebleed_site}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) corresponding to the location of bleeding/haemorrhage site(s).', NULL, 101842),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severebleed_oth}', 'question', 'If other: Specify other site(s) of bleeding', NULL, 101843),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severebleed_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the location of bleeding/haemorrhage site(s).', NULL, 101844),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_severebleed_oth}', 'completionGuide', 'If ''Other'', Write the other location of site(s) where the patient has experienced bleeding/haemorrhage at any time from onset of this illness and presentation or admission.', NULL, 101845),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_coagulatio}', 'question', 'Coagulation disorder / DIC', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101846),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_coagulatio}', 'definition', 'Coagulopathy (bleeding disorder) is defined as a condition in which there is a deviation from or interruption of the normal coagulation properties of the blood (normal blood clotting is disrupted). Disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC) is defined as a pathological process where the blood starts to coagulate throughout the whole body. Acute DIC is confirmed by demonstrating increased thrombin generation (e.g. decreased fibrinogen) and increased fibrinolysis (e.g. elevated fibrin degradation products and D-dimer). The diagnosis of chronic DIC may be largely based upon evidence of microangiopathy on the blood film and increased levels of fibrin degradation products and particularly D-dimer.', NULL, 101847),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_coagulatio}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101848),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_acuterenal}', 'question', 'Acute renal injury / acute renal failure', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101849),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_acuterenal}', 'definition', 'Acute kidney injury is defined when one of the following criteria is met: Serum creatinine rises by >= 26umol/L or 0.3mg/dL within 48 hours; or serum creatinine rises >= 1.5 fold from the reference value, which is known or presumed to have occurred within the prior 7 days; or urine output is <0.5ml/kg/hr for >6 consecutive hours.', NULL, 101850),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_acuterenal}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101851),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_uti}', 'question', 'Urinary tract infection', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101852),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_uti}', 'definition', 'This refers to inflammatory responses of the epithelium of the urinary tract to microbial invasions. They are often bacterial infections with associated bacteruria and pyuria.', NULL, 101853),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_rhabdomyol}', 'definition', 'Rhabdomyolysis is a syndrome characterised by muscle necrosis and the release of myoglobin into the blood, resulting from muscle injury. Diagnosis is made in a patient with either an acute neuromuscular illness or dark urine without other symptoms, plus a marked acute elevation in creatine kinase. The creatine kinase is typically at least five times the upper limit of normal (there is no diagnostic threshold to establish the diagnosis, however). Muscle biopsy, electromyography, radiological imaging and the presence of myoglobinuria are not required for the diagnosis.', NULL, 101856),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_rhabdomyol}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101857),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_myositis}', 'question', 'Myositis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101858),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_myositis}', 'definition', 'Myositis is defined as an inflammatory process affecting the skeletal muscles. Causes include infections, injuries, and autoimmune disorders. It may be a clinical diagnosis with supporting evidence from laboratory tests e.g. elevated serum creatine kinase; histological confirmation is not required to make the diagnosis. Myositis can occur without subsequent progression to rhabdomyolysis.', NULL, 101859),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_myositis}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101860),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cellulitis_yn}', 'question', 'Cellulitis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101861),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cellulitis_yn}', 'definition', 'Defined as an acute, diffuse, and suppurative inflammation of loose connective tissue, particularly the deep subcutaneous tissues, and sometimes muscle, which is most commonly seen as a result of infection. Diagnosis is made on clinical signs and symptoms, it can be supported by microbiological evidence.', NULL, 101862),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cellulitis_yn}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101863),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cellulitis_site}', 'question', 'If yes: Site(s) of cellulitis', '{Skin,Nose,Gums,"GI tract","Urinary tract",Vagina,Other,Unknown}', 101864),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cellulitis_site}', 'definition', 'This refers to the site(s) in which cellulitis was identified.', NULL, 101865),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cellulitis_site}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate site(s) in which cellulitis was identified at any time during hospitalisation. If ''Other'', Specify the other site(s) in the space provided below.', NULL, 101866),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cellulitis_other}', 'question', 'If other: Specify other site(s) of cellulitis', NULL, 101867),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cellulitis_other}', 'definition', 'This refers to the other site(s) in which cellulitis was identified.', NULL, 101868),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_cellulitis_other}', 'completionGuide', 'If ''Other'', write the site(s) in which cellulitis was identified at any time during hospitalisation. ', NULL, 101869),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_eschar}', 'question', 'Skin tissue loss or eschar', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101870),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_eschar}', 'definition', 'Eschar is defined as a dry, dark scab or falling away of dead skin, typically caused by a burn, an insect bite (e.g. some rickettsial infections), or infection with anthrax.', NULL, 101871),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_eschar}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101872),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_bacteraemi}', 'question', 'Bacteraemia', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101873),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_bacteraemi}', 'definition', 'Defined as the presence of bacteria in blood, most often detected through blood culture investigation. Episodes of suspected artefactual contamination of a blood culture should not be recorded.', NULL, 101874),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_bacteraemi}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'' if bacteraemia occurred at any time during hospitalisation. Indicate ''No'', if bacteraemia never occurred or if only bacteria grown were believed to be skin contaminants (e.g. coagulase negative Staphylococci or diphtheroids).', NULL, 101875),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_hyperglyce}', 'question', 'Hyperglycemia', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101876),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_hyperglyce}', 'definition', 'For adults, is defined as an abnormally high level of glucose in the blood, blood glucose level that is consistently above 126mg/dL or 7 mmol/L. For children, is defined as a blood glucose level consistently above 8.3 mmol/L.', NULL, 101877),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_hypoglycem}', 'question', 'Hypoglycaemia', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101878),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_hypoglycem}', 'definition', 'This refers to abnormally low level of glucose in the blood. For adults, is defined as an abnormally low level of glucose in the blood, a blood glucose level that is consistently below 70mg/dL or 4 mmol/L. For children, is defined as a blood glucose level below 3 mmol/L.', NULL, 101879),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_hypoglycem}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101880),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_shock}', 'question', 'Shock', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101881),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_shock}', 'definition', 'Shock refers to circulatory failure, causing inadequate oxygen delivery to meet cellular metabolic needs. It is defined by the presence of any two of the following: evidence of hypoperfusion (e.g. capillary refill >2 seconds, cold clammy skin, and rapid/weak pulse, altered mental status), narrow pulse pressure (less than or equal to 20mmHg), hypotension for age, and tachycardia (>100bpm).', NULL, 101882),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_shock}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101883),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_reshock}', 'question', 'Re-shock episodes', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101884),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_reshock}', 'definition', 'Re-shock or recurrent shock is defined as a separate episode of shock which occurs at least 2-6 hours after the clinical resolution of an initial episode of shock, where clinical resolution refers to a pulse pressure >25mmHg without signs of impaired perfusion. This does not include persistent shock (where no resolution is seen).', NULL, 101885),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_reshock}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101886),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_reshockep}', 'question', 'Number of re-shock episodes', '{1,2,3,4+,Unknown}', 101887),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_reshockep}', 'definition', 'This refers to the number of times re-shock was identified while the patient was hospitalised.', NULL, 101888),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_reshockep}', 'completionGuide', 'If ''Yes'', select the single most appropriate option which corresponds to the number of re-shock episodes the patient has experienced at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101889),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_sepsis}', 'question', 'Sepsis', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101890),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_sepsis}', 'definition', 'As defined according to the 2016 SCCM/ESICM task force as a life-threatening organ dysfunction caused by a dysregulated host response to infection with the following: Organ dysfunction determined by a Sequential Organ Failure Assessment (SOFA) score of greater or equal to 2 points (or quick SOFA/qSOFA score of greater or equal to 2); and a Physician-diagnosed infection (which can be supported by clinical signs and symptoms, radiologic and/or microbiologic evidence).', NULL, 101891),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_sepsis}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101892),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_unlisted}', 'question', 'Other complication(s)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101893),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_unlisted}', 'definition', 'This refers to other complication(s) not specified above.', NULL, 101894),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,compl_unlisted}', 'completionGuide', 'Specify all other complication(s), not listed above, the patient experienced at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101895),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid}', 'question', 'PARENTERAL / IV FLUID', NULL, 101896),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_occur}', 'question', 'Parenteral / IV fluid', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101897),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_occur}', 'definition', 'This refers to intravenous fluid which includes crystalloid, albumin, gelatin, starches or other solutions.', NULL, 101898),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_occur}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient received intravenous fluids at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101899),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_type}', 'question', 'If yes: Select all parenteral / IV fluid that were administered', '{Crystalloid,Albumin,Gelatin,Starches,Other}', 101900),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of parenteral or intravenous (IV) fluid is prescribed as a replacement of fluid, electrolytes, calories, vitamins, and other nutritional substances. Crystalloid fluids refers to solutions of mineral salts, including normal (0.9%) saline, Lactated Ringer''s/Hartman''s solution, 5% dextrose in water, 10% dextrose in water, hypotonic and hypertonic saline, among others. Albumin refers to intravenous preparations of purified human serum albumin used to replace lost albumin in patients with hypoalbuminemia, to treat hypovolemia and ascites, and as a part of some diagnostic imaging kits. Common albumin colloid solutions include Albumin 4%, 5% and 20% among others. Gelatin refers to a colloidal, isotonic, physiologically balanced, plasma volume substitute containing succinylated gelatine and electrolytes, with potential nephroprotective properties. Common gelatin parenteral fluids include Gelaspan, Gelofusine, Geloplasma, Isoplex, among others. Starches refers to an intravenous solution of hydroxyethyl starch (HES), synthetic, nonionic hydroxyethyl derivative of starch used as a plasma expander when prepared in an isotonic solution. Common starch based, synthetic colloid, parenteral fluids include hydroxyethyl starch (HES) products, among others.', NULL, 101901),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_type}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) corresponding to the parenteral fluid(s) administered.', NULL, 101902),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_cryst}', 'question', 'Total crystalloid volume given during admission (mL)', NULL, 101903),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_cryst}', 'definition', 'Crystalloid fluids refers to solutions of mineral salts, including normal (0.9%) saline, Lactated Ringer''s/Hartman''s solution, 5% dextrose in water, 10% dextrose in water, hypotonic and hypertonic saline, among others.', NULL, 101904),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_cryst}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the total volume of crystalloid fluid the patient received during admission in millilitres (mL).', NULL, 101905),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_albu}', 'question', 'Total albumin volume given during admission (mL)', NULL, 101906),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_albu}', 'definition', 'Albumin refers to intravenous preparations of purified human serum albumin used to replace lost albumin in patients with hypoalbuminemia, to treat hypovolemia and ascites, and as a part of some diagnostic imaging kits. Common albumin colloid solutions include Albumin 4%, 5% and 20% among others.', NULL, 101907),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_albu}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the total volume of albumin fluid the patient received during admission in millilitres (mL).', NULL, 101908),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_gelat}', 'question', 'Total gelatin volume given during admission (mL)', NULL, 101909),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_gelat}', 'definition', 'Gelatin refers to a colloidal, isotonic, physiologically balanced, plasma volume substitute containing succinylated gelatine and electrolytes, with potential nephroprotective properties. Common gelatin parenteral fluids include Gelaspan, Gelofusine, Geloplasma, Isoplex, among others.', NULL, 101910),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_gelat}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the total volume of gelatin fluid the patient received during admission in millilitres (mL).', NULL, 101911),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_star}', 'question', 'Total starches volume given during admission (mL)', NULL, 101912),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_star}', 'definition', 'Starches refers to an intravenous solution of hydroxyethyl starch (HES), synthetic, nonionic hydroxyethyl derivative of starch used as a plasma expander when prepared in an isotonic solution. Common starch based, synthetic colloid, parenteral fluids include hydroxyethyl starch (HES) products, among others.', NULL, 101913),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_star}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the total volume of starches the patient received during admission in millilitres (mL).', NULL, 101914),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_oth}', 'question', 'If other: Specify other fluid', NULL, 101915),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of other fluids the patient received, not mentioned above.', NULL, 101916),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_oth}', 'completionGuide', 'Write the other type of fluid the patient received during admission in millilitres (mL).', NULL, 101917),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_othv}', 'question', 'Total volume given during admission (mL)', NULL, 101918),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_othv}', 'definition', 'This refers to the volume of other fluids the patient received, not mentioned above.', NULL, 101919),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_othv}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the volume of other fluid the patient received during admission in millilitres (mL).', NULL, 101920),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_reas}', 'question', 'Reason(s) for IV fluid (check all that apply)', '{Shock,"High/rising haematocrit",Anorexia,"Persistent vomiting",Other}', 101921),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_reas}', 'definition', 'This refers to the reason(s) (indication(s)) for parenteral / intravenous (IV) fluid therapy at any time during the admission. If multiple indications, select all that apply. Shock refers to circulatory failure, causing inadequate oxygen delivery to meet cellular metabolic needs. It is defined by the presence of any two of the following: evidence of hypoperfusion (e.g. capillary refill >2 seconds, cold clammy skin, and rapid/weak pulse, altered mental status), narrow pulse pressure (less than or equal to 20mmHg), hypotension for age, and tachycardia (>100bpm). High/rising haematorit refers to an elevation above the normal ratio of the volume of red blood cells to the total volume of blood. Anorexia refers to the lack or loss of appetite accompanied by an aversion to food and the inability to eat. ', NULL, 101922),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_reas}', 'completionGuide', 'Select all that apply.', NULL, 101923),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_reasoth}', 'question', 'If other: Specify other reason for IV fluid', NULL, 101924),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_reasoth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the reason(s) (indication(s)) for parenteral / intravenous (IV) fluid therapy at any time during the admission.', NULL, 101925),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_reasoth}', 'completionGuide', 'If ''Other'', specify the reason(s) (indication(s)) for parenteral / intravenous (IV) fluid therapy at any time during the admission.', NULL, 101926),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_start}', 'question', 'Date first IV fluid started', NULL, 101927),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_start}', 'definition', 'This refers to the date when the first parenteral / intravenous (IV) fluid was started.', NULL, 101928),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_start}', 'completionGuide', 'Enter the date in DD/MM/YYYY format.', NULL, 101929),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_end}', 'question', 'Date last IV fluid ended', NULL, 101930),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_end}', 'definition', 'This refers to the date when the last parenteral / intravenous (IV) fluid was ended.', NULL, 101931),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivfluid_end}', 'completionGuide', 'Enter the date in DD/MM/YYYY format.', NULL, 101932),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt}', 'question', 'BLOOD PRODUCT TRANSFUSION', NULL, 101933),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_yn}', 'question', 'Blood product transfusion', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101934),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_yn}', 'definition', 'This refers to a transfusion of blood (whole blood or packed red blood cells) or other blood products excluding human normal immunoglobulin (e.g. albumin, granulocytes, platelets, fresh-frozen plasma (FFP), FP24, PF-24, cryoprecipitate, protein C concentrate, cryosupernatant, or a specific non-recombinant clotting factor) at any time on the date of assessment. ', NULL, 101935),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_yn}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient received blood products or blood product transfusion at any time during admission. If ''Yes'' Select the product(s) below.', NULL, 101936),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_type}', 'question', 'If yes: Select all blood product transfusion that were administered', '{Platelets,Cryoprecipitate,"Whole blood/packed RBC","Frozen fresh plasma","Fibrinogen concentrate"}', 101937),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to a transfusion of blood (whole blood or packed red blood cells) or other blood products excluding human normal immunoglobulin (e.g. albumin, granulocytes, platelets, fresh-frozen plasma (FFP), FP24, PF-24, cryoprecipitate, protein C concentrate, cryosupernatant, or a specific non-recombinant clotting factor) at any time on the date of assessment. Platelets refers to the transfer of blood platelets from a donor to a recipient or reinfusion to the donor. Cryoprecipitate refers to a frozen blood product prepared from frozen plasma that contains fibrinogen (factor I), antihemophilic factor (factor VIII), factor XIII, von Willebrand factor (vWF) and fibronectin. Whole blood refers to intravenous administration of whole blood (blood that contains plasma and red blood cells) into an individual. Packed RBC refers to red blood cells from a unit of whole blood following removal of most of the plasma, leaving a unit with a haematocrit of about 60%. Fresh frozen plasma refers to the plasma that is separated from the whole blood and frozen quickly after a blood donation in order to be used for blood transfusions. Fibrinogen concentrate is a haemostatic agent used for the treatment of acute bleeding episodes in patients with congenital fibrinogen deficiency, including afibrinogenemia and hypofibrinogenemia.', NULL, 101938),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_type}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) corresponding to the blood product(s) that were administered.', NULL, 101939),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_plate}', 'question', 'Platelets, total number of units', NULL, 101940),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_plate}', 'definition', 'Platelets refers to the transfer of blood platelets from a donor to a recipient or reinfusion to the donor.', NULL, 101941),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_plate}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the total number of units the patient received during admission.', NULL, 101942),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_cryo}', 'question', 'Cryoprecipitate, total number of units', NULL, 101943),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_suppleo2}', 'definition', 'This refers to any method of oxygen therapy that may be delivered via nose cannula, mask or non-invasive or invasive ventilation.', NULL, 101977),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_cryo}', 'definition', 'Cryoprecipitate refers to a frozen blood product prepared from frozen plasma that contains fibrinogen (factor I), antihemophilic factor (factor VIII), factor XIII, von Willebrand factor (vWF) and fibronectin. Cryoprecipitate refers to a frozen blood product prepared from frozen plasma that contains fibrinogen (factor I), antihemophilic factor (factor VIII), factor XIII, von Willebrand factor (vWF) and fibronectin.', NULL, 101944),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_cryo}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the total number of units the patient received during admission.', NULL, 101945),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_rbc}', 'question', 'Whole blood/packed RBC, total number of units', NULL, 101946),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_rbc}', 'definition', 'Whole blood refers to intravenous administration of whole blood (blood that contains plasma and red blood cells) into an individual. Packed RBC refers to red blood cells from a unit of whole blood following removal of most of the plasma, leaving a unit with a haematocrit of about 60%.', NULL, 101947),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_rbc}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the total number of units the patient received during admission.', NULL, 101948),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_ffp}', 'question', 'Fresh frozen plasma (FFP), total number of units', NULL, 101949),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_ffp}', 'definition', 'Fresh frozen plasma refers to the plasma that is separated from the whole blood and frozen quickly after a blood donation in order to be used for blood transfusions.', NULL, 101950),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_ffp}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the total number of units the patient received during admission.', NULL, 101951),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_fibrin}', 'question', 'Fibrinogen concentrate, total number of units', NULL, 101952),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_fibrin}', 'definition', 'Fibrinogen concentrate is a hemostatic agent used for the treatment of acute bleeding episodes in patients with congenital fibrinogen deficiency, including afibrinogenemia and hypofibrinogenemia.', NULL, 101953),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_bpt_fibrin}', 'completionGuide', 'Record the total number of units the patient received during admission.', NULL, 101954),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivimmunogl}', 'question', 'Intravenous immunoglobulin', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101955),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivimmunogl}', 'definition', 'This refers to immunoglobulin preparations used in intravenous infusion, containing primarily Immunoglobulin G (IgG).Examples of commercial intravenous immunoglobulin IVIG preparations include Octagam®, Intragam P®, KIOVIG®, Flebogamma 5% DIF®, Carimune NF®, Gamunex®, Gammagard S/D®, Gammagard Liquid®, Gammaked® and Privigen®.', NULL, 101956),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ivimmunogl}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient received intravenous immunoglobulin at any time during admission.', NULL, 101957),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_diuretics}', 'question', 'Diuretics', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101958),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_diuretics}', 'definition', 'This refers to class of agents that increases the production of urine by the kidney. Via various mechanism of actions, diuretics retain water in urine, thus provides a means of forced diuresis.', NULL, 101959),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_diuretics}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient received diuretic therapy at any time during admission.', NULL, 101960),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_nacetylcys}', 'question', 'N-acetyl cysteine', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101961),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_nacetylcys}', 'definition', 'This refers to N-acetyl derivative of cysteine; used as a mucolytic agent to reduce the viscosity of mucous secretions.', NULL, 101962),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_nacetylcys}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient received N-acetyl cysteine (NAC) at any time during admission.', NULL, 101963),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_fluiddrain}', 'question', 'Fluid drainage', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101964),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_fluiddrain}', 'definition', 'This refers to the procedure of removing fluid from the pleural space or peritoneal cavity.', NULL, 101965),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_fluiddrain}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if this was fluid drainage from the pleural or peritoneal cavity was performed at any time during admission.', NULL, 101966),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_fluiddrain_reas}', 'question', 'If yes: Reason for this drainage', '{Ascites,"Pleural effusion"}', 101967),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_fluiddrain_reas}', 'definition', 'This refers to the reason (indication) for fluid drainage. Ascites refers to the abnormal accumulation of fluid in the peritoneal cavity. Pleural effusion refers to presence of fluid in the pleural cavity resulting from excessive transudation or exudation from the pleural surfaces.', NULL, 101968),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_fluiddrain_reas}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option corresponding to the reason (indication) for fluid drainage.', NULL, 101969),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_plasmaex}', 'question', 'Plasmapheresis / plasma exchange', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101970),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_plasmaex}', 'definition', 'Plasmapheresis (plasma exchange) refers to the extracorporeal separation of blood components, resulting in a filtered product. Methods include discontinuous flow centrifugation, continuous flow centrifugation and plasma filtration.', NULL, 101971),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_plasmaex}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient received plasmapharesis at any time during admission.', NULL, 101972),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_plasmadur}', 'question', 'If yes: Days on plasma exchange support during admission', NULL, 101973),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_plasmadur}', 'definition', 'This refers to the total number of calendar days the patient was on plasma exchange support (plasmapharesis). Plasmapheresis (plasma exchange) refers to the extracorporeal separation of blood components, resulting in a filtered product. Methods include discontinuous flow centrifugation, continuous flow centrifugation and plasma filtration.', NULL, 101974),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_plasmadur}', 'completionGuide', 'Write the total number of calendar days the patient was on plasma exchange support (plasmaphe\resis).', NULL, 101975),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_suppleo2}', 'question', 'Any supplemental oxygen?', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 101976),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_suppleo2}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101978),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_o2support_type}', 'question', 'If yes: Select all types of respiratory support the patient received', '{"Nasal prong","Face mask","High-flow nasal oxygen","Non-invasive ventilation","Invasive ventilation","ECLS/ ECMO",Unknown}', 101979),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_o2support_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the mode in which the patient received supplemental oxygen at any time during hospitalisation. Non-invasive ventilation refers to the provision of ventilatory support through the patient''s upper airway using a mask or similar device. Invasive ventilation means that patient has undergone tracheal intubation, for the purpose of invasive mechanical ventilation. Invasive ventilation is a method to mechanically assist or replace spontaneous breathing in patients by use of a powered device that forces oxygenated air into the lungs. The mode of intubation may be orotracheal, nasotracheal, or via a cricothyrotomy or tracheotomy. Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation (ECMO) also called to as Extracorporeal life support (ECLS) refers to application of a life support system that circulates the blood through an oxygenating system, which may consist of a pump, a membrane oxygenator, and a heat exchanger.', NULL, 101980),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_o2support_type}', 'completionGuide', 'Select all types of respiratory support the patient received at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101981),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_suppleo2_flow}', 'question', 'Maximum O2 flow volume (L/min)', '{"<2 L/min","2-5 L/min","6-10 L/min","11-15 L/min",">15 L/min",Unknown}', 101982),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_suppleo2_flow}', 'definition', 'This refers to the maximum flow volume of O2 delivered to the patient at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101983),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_suppleo2_flow}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the maximum flow volume of O2 delivered to the patient at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 101984),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_o2therapyd}', 'question', 'Number of calendar days the patient received any respiratory support during admission', NULL, 101985),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_o2therapyd}', 'definition', 'This refers to the total number of calendar days the patient received this respiratory support during admission (includes use at any time during admission).', NULL, 101986),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_o2therapyd}', 'completionGuide', 'Write the total number of calendar days the patient received this respiratory support during admission (includes use at any time during admission).', NULL, 101987),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_hfnodur}', 'question', 'Number of calendar days the patient received high-flow nasal oxygen', NULL, 101988),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_hfnodur}', 'definition', 'This refers to the total number of calendar days the patient received high-flow nasal oxygen.', NULL, 101989),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_hfnodur}', 'completionGuide', 'Write the total number of calendar days the patient received high-flow nasal oxygen during admission (includes use at any time during admission).', NULL, 101990),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_nivent}', 'question', 'Type of non-invasive ventilation', '{CPAP,BIPAP,Other,Unknown}', 101991),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_nivent}', 'definition', 'Non-invasive respiratory support or ventilation (NIV) refers to the provision of ventilatory support through the patient''s upper airway using a mask or similar device. It includes high-flow nasal cannula, continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP) and bilevel positive airway pressure (BPAP).', NULL, 101992),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_nivent}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option corresponding to the type of non-invasive ventilation used. ', NULL, 101993),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_nivent_oth}', 'question', 'If other: Specify type of non-invasive ventilation', NULL, 101994),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ninventdur}', 'question', 'Number of calendar days the patient received non-invasive ventilation', NULL, 101995),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ninventdur}', 'definition', 'This refers to the total number of calendar days the patient received non-invasive ventilation.', NULL, 101996),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ninventdur}', 'completionGuide', 'Write the total number of calendar days the patient received non-invasive ventilation during admission (includes use at any time during admission).', NULL, 101997),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_inventdur}', 'question', 'Number of calendar days the patient received invasive ventilation', NULL, 101998),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_inventdur}', 'definition', 'This refers to the total number of calendar days the patient received invasive ventilation.', NULL, 101999),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_inventdur}', 'completionGuide', 'Write the total number of calendar days the patient received invasive ventilation during admission (includes use at any time during admission).', NULL, 102000),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ecmo}', 'question', 'Type of ECLS / ECMO', '{"Veno-venous (VV)","Veno-arterial (VA)",Unknown}', 102001),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ecmo}', 'definition', 'The two main types of Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation (ECMO), also called Extracorporeal life support (ECLS), are veno-venous (venous-venous), which is used to support the lungs and veno-arterial (venous-arterial), which is used to support the lungs and heart.', NULL, 102002),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ecmo}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option corresponding to the type of Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation (ECMO) / Extracorporeal life support (ECLS) used. ', NULL, 102003),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ecmodur}', 'question', 'Number of calendar days the patient received ECLS / ECMO', NULL, 102004),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ecmodur}', 'definition', 'This refers to the number of calendar days the patient received Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation (ECMO), also called Extracorporeal life support (ECLS).', NULL, 102005),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_ecmodur}', 'completionGuide', 'Write the total number of calendar days the patient received ECLS/ECMO during admission (includes use at any time during admission).', NULL, 102006),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_prone_yn}', 'question', 'Prone positioning', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 102007),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_prone_yn}', 'definition', 'Prone positioning refers to the act of having the patient lying in the prone position to assist ventilation. This includes both invasive ventilation/intubated patients and non-intubated or self-ventilating patients. ', NULL, 102008),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_prone_yn}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', for any patients if they have been in the prone position to aid their ventilation at any time during admission. ', NULL, 102009),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_isolation}', 'question', 'Was the patient isolated at home or in hospital?', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 102010),
	('2026-03-24 08:40:04.3022+00', '{ARC,inter_isolation}', 'definition', 'This refers to isolation of the patient at home or in hospital during this admission for pathogen of interest.', NULL, 102011),
