	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_paed}', 'question', 'Paediatric-specific signs', NULL, 102856),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_dist}', 'definition', 'This refers to the pattern of distribution of the skin rash. Generalised rash refers to a widespread rash covering the entire surface of the skin. Centrifugal rash is concentrated on the distal extremities, with fewer lesions on the trunk. Centripetal rash is concentrated on the trunk, with fewer lesions on the extremities. Localised around the genitals refers to a rash concentrated around the skin on the genitals.', NULL, 102857),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_dist}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate pattern of distribution of the skin rash on the day of assessment.', NULL, 102858),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_distoth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the pattern of distribution of the skin rash.', NULL, 102859),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_distoth}', 'completionGuide', 'If ''Other'', write the pattern of distribution of the skin rash on the day of assessment.', NULL, 102860),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_morph}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate morphology of the skin rash on the day of assessment.', NULL, 102861),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_skinles}', 'definition', 'This refers to the status of the skin lesions. Active skin lesions refer to macules (flat lesions), papules (raised lesions), vesicles (raised and filled with clear fluid) or pustules (raised and filed with pus, an opaque fluid) which can develop a depression in the centre (umbilication) or ulcerate. Skin lesions which are not active refer to those which have begun to crust (dry) over, in the process of healing & resolving, to form scabs (consisting of dried serum, blood, or pus). Skin lesions which have completely resolved refer to all scabs having fallen off, leaving intact underlying skin.', NULL, 102862),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_skinles}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate the most appropriate dermatological status of the skin lesions on the day of assessment.', NULL, 102863),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_head_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the head, face or neck. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface.', NULL, 102864),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_ocular}', 'definition', 'This refers to the presence of ocular lesions.', NULL, 102865),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_ocular_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of ocular lesion. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface.', NULL, 102866),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_ocular_type_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of ocular lesion.', NULL, 102867),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_torso_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the torso / trunk. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface.', NULL, 102868),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_torso_type_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the torso / trunk.', NULL, 102869),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_arms_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the arms and/or hands. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface.', NULL, 102870),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_arms_type_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the arms and/or hands.', NULL, 102871),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_legs_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the legs and/or feet. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface.', NULL, 102872),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_legs_type_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the legs and/or feet.', NULL, 102873),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_palm_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the palms. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface.', NULL, 102874),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_palm_type_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the palms.', NULL, 102875),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_sole_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the soles. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface.', NULL, 102876),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_sole_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the soles.', NULL, 102877),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_genit_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the external genitalia. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface.', NULL, 102878),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_genit_type_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the external genitalia.', NULL, 102879),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_peri_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the perianal region. Vesicle refers to raised lesion and filled with clear fluid. Pustule refers to raised lesion and filed with pus, an opaque fluid. Ulcerated lesion refers to a lesion with break in the skin. Necrotising lesion refers to a lesion with necrotic (dead) tissue. Fungating lesion refers to a lesion from underlying tissues which is breaking through the skin''s surface.', NULL, 102880),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_peri_type_oth}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of skin lesions involving the perianal region.', NULL, 102881),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"SKIN & MUCOSA ASSESSMENT: Record the information furthest from normal between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lesion_desc}', 'definition', 'This refers to other lesion complication(s) which have not been specified above.', NULL, 102882),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"TREATMENTS & INTERVENTIONS: Record all interventions given between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",treat_blood_whole}', 'definition', 'Whole blood refers to intravenous administration of whole blood (blood that contains plasma and red blood cells) into an individual.', NULL, 102883),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"JOINT ASSESSMENT",joint_crp}', 'question', 'CRP — C-Reactive Protein (mg/L)', NULL, 103166),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"TREATMENTS & INTERVENTIONS: Record all interventions given between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",treat_intravenim}', 'definition', 'This refers to immunoglobulin preparations, containing primarily Immunoglobulin G (IgG), that are used as intravenous infusions. Examples: Octagam®, Intragam P®, KIOVIG®, Flebogamma 5% DIF®, Carimune NF®, Gamunex®, Gammagard S/D®, Gammagard Liquid®, Gammaked® and Privigen®.', NULL, 102884),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"TREATMENTS & INTERVENTIONS: Record all interventions given between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",treat_other_spec}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'' if other intervention(s) or procedure(s) were used between 00:00 and 24:00 hours on day of assessment.', NULL, 102885),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"RESPIRATORY SUPPORT: Record all respiratory interventions given between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",treat_niv}', 'definition', 'This refers to non-invasive ventilation which provides ventilatory support through the patient''s upper airway using a mask or similar device, without the need for tracheal intubation. Examples include Continuous Positive Airway Pressure (CPAP) and Biphasic Continuous Positive Airway Pressure (BiPAP).', NULL, 102886),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"RESPIRATORY SUPPORT: Record all respiratory interventions given between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",treat_prone}', 'definition', 'This refers to prone positioning which is the act of having the patient lying in the prone position to assist ventilation. It may be implemented for patients on invasive ventilation (intubated) as well as non-intubated or self-ventilating patients.', NULL, 102887),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,daily,"RESPIRATORY SUPPORT: Record all respiratory interventions given between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",treat_prone_when}', 'definition', 'This refers to prone positioning which is the act of having the patient lying in the prone position to assist ventilation. It may be implemented for patients on invasive ventilation (intubated) as well as non-intubated or self-ventilating patients.', NULL, 102888),
