	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,photographs,PHOTOGRAPHS,photo_sampleid}', 'definition', 'Refers to identification number (ID) of the sample.', NULL, 103110),
	('2026-06-22 13:22:38.600013+00', '{Lists,drugs,Antibiotics,Dirithromycin}', 'listItem', 'Dirithromycin', NULL, 104111),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_gbs}', 'definition', 'Refers to a rapidly progressive autoimmune disorder of the peripheral nervous system characterized by limb paresthesias, areflexia, and generalized muscle weakness or paralysis that often begins in the legs and spreads to the arms, torso, and face.', NULL, 103111),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_atm}', 'question', 'Acute Transverse Myelitis (ATM)', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 103112),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_atm}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 103113),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_perneur}', 'question', 'Peripheral neuropathy', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 103114),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_perneur}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 103115),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_ards}', 'definition', 'Acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) is a non-cardiogenic pulmonary oedema and diffuse lung inflammation syndrome that often complicates critical illness. Diagnosis of ARDS is based on fulfilling three criteria: a) Acute onset (within 1 week) b) Bilateral opacities on chest radiography or computed tomography (CT), or bilateral B lines and/or consolidations on ultrasound not fully explained by effusions, atelectasis, or nodules/masses. c)PaO2/FiO2 (arterial to inspired oxygen) ratio of ?300 or SpO2/FiO2 (pulse oximetric saturation to inspired oxygen) ratio of ?315.', NULL, 103116),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_jaundice}', 'definition', 'This refers to a clinical manifestation of hyperbilirubinemia, characterized by the yellowish staining of the skin, mucous membrane and/or sclera.', NULL, 103117),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_thrombemb_spec}', 'completionGuide', 'If ''Other'', write the other thromboembolic diagnoses the patient experienced at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 103118),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_cellulitis_site_oth}', 'completionGuide', 'If ''Other'', write the site(s) in which cellulitis was identified at any time during hospitalisation.', NULL, 103119),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_ndiab}', 'question', 'New-onset diabetes mellitus', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 103120),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"COMPLICATIONS: Experienced at any time from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",compl_plarthalgia}', 'question', 'Polyartralgia', '{Yes,No,Unknown}', 103121),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"INTERVENTIONS: Record interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_ivfluid_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of parenteral or intravenous (IV) fluid is prescribed as a replacement of fluid, electrolytes, calories, vitamins, and other nutritional substances. Intravenous fluids may be crystalloids (commonly including 0.9% Sodium Chloride (Normal Saline), Lactated Ringer(USP), 0.45% Sodium Chloride (Half-normal saline), 0.45% normal saline + 4% Glucose (Half-normal saline with dextrose), 0.18%-0.3% Sodium Chloride + 4% Glucose (Hypotonic saline with dextrose), 5% Glucose (Dextrose 5% in Water), Ringeracetate or Plasmalyte) or colloids (commonly including gelatins, starches or albumin).', NULL, 103122),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"INTERVENTIONS: Record interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_ivfluid_colloid}', 'definition', 'Colloid fluids are solutions that contain large molecules, such as proteins or polysaccharides, which remain in the bloodstream for a longer duration compared to crystalloids. These fluids help maintain or expand intravascular volume by drawing water into the blood vessels via oncotic pressure. Common colloids include gelatins, starches or albumin.', NULL, 103123),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"INTERVENTIONS: Record interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_ivfluid_reas}', 'definition', 'This refers to the reason(s) (indication(s)) for parenteral / intravenous (IV) fluid therapy at any time during the admission. If multiple indications, select all that apply. Shock refers to circulatory failure, causing inadequate oxygen delivery to meet cellular metabolic needs. It is defined by the presence of any two of the following: evidence of hypoperfusion (e.g. capillary refill >2 seconds, cold clammy skin, and rapid/weak pulse, altered mental status), narrow pulse pressure (less than or equal to 20mmHg), hypotension for age, and tachycardia (>100bpm). High/rising haematorit refers to an elevation above the normal ratio of the volume of red blood cells to the total volume of blood. Anorexia refers to the lack or loss of appetite accompanied by an aversion to food and the inability to eat.', NULL, 103124),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"INTERVENTIONS: Record interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_bpt}', 'definition', 'This refers to a transfusion of blood (whole blood or packed red blood cells) or other blood products excluding human normal immunoglobulin (e.g. albumin, granulocytes, platelets, fresh-frozen plasma (FFP), FP24, PF-24, cryoprecipitate, protein C concentrate, cryosupernatant, or a specific non-recombinant clotting factor) at any time on the date of assessment.', NULL, 103125),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"INTERVENTIONS: Record interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_bpt_rbc}', 'definition', 'Whole blood refers to intravenous administration of whole blood (blood that contains plasma and red blood cells) into an individual.', NULL, 103126),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"INTERVENTIONS: Record interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_other}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'' if other intervention(s) or procedure(s) were used between 00:00 and 24:00 hours on day of assessment.', NULL, 103127),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,pregnancy,"PREGNANCY-RELATED COMPLICATIONS",pregcomp_pih_week}', 'question', 'Gestational week of onset', NULL, 103239),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"RESPIRATORY SUPPORT: Record all respiratory interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_nivent}', 'definition', 'This refers to the mode in which the patient received supplemental oxygen on day of assessment. Non-invasive ventilation refers to the provision of ventilatory support through the patient''s upper airway using a mask or similar device, without the need for tracheal intubation. Examples include Continuous Positive Airway Pressure (CPAP) and Biphasic Continuous Positive Airway Pressure (BiPAP).', NULL, 103128),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"RESPIRATORY SUPPORT: Record all respiratory interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_prone}', 'definition', 'Prone positioning refers to the act of having the patient lying in the prone position to assist ventilation. This includes both invasive ventilation/intubated patients and non-intubated or self-ventilating patients.', NULL, 103129),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"RESPIRATORY SUPPORT: Record all respiratory interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_prone}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', for any patients if they have been in the prone position to aid their ventilation at any time during admission.', NULL, 103130),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,"RESPIRATORY SUPPORT: Record all respiratory interventions given or prescribed from day of presentation to day of discharge / outcome.",inter_prone_when}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of assisted ventilation when the patient was placed in prone position. This may be either invasive ventilation / intubated patients or non-intubated / self-ventilating patients.', NULL, 103131),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,DIAGNOSIS,diagn_dengueclass}', 'definition', 'This refers to the 2009, World Health Organisation dengue classification.', NULL, 103132),
	('2026-04-20 13:35:28.186514+00', '{ARC,outcome,DIAGNOSIS,diagn_hepatitis_type_oth}', 'completionGuide', 'If ''Other'', specify the type of Hepatitis virus.', NULL, 103133),
