	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,presentation,"CO-MORBIDITIES AND RISK FACTORS: Existing prior to this current illness and is ongoing",comor_rheumatolo_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to rheumatologic disorders. Osteoarthritis is a disabling joint disease characterized by degeneration of the joint complex that can have various causes, most notably advanced age and overuse. Rheumatoid Arthritis is a chronic, systemic autoimmune disorder characterized by inflammation in the synovial membranes and articular surfaces. Systemic Lupus Erythematosus is a chronic, relapsing, inflammatory, and often febrile multisystemic disorder of connective tissue, characterized principally by involvement of the skin, joints, kidneys, and serosal membranes. Ankylosing Spondylitis is a chronic inflammatory disease of the axial skeleton that leads to partial or complete vertebral fusion and spine rigidity. Psoriatic Arthritis is a seronegative inflammatory arthritis found in patients with psoriasis.', NULL, 104318),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,presentation,"CO-MORBIDITIES AND RISK FACTORS: Existing prior to this current illness and is ongoing",comor_rheumatolo_type}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) which represent the rheumatologic disorder(s) experienced by the individual.', NULL, 104319),
