	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,presentation,"CO-MORBIDITIES AND RISK FACTORS: Existing prior to this current illness and is ongoing",medic_headinf_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to specific types infections affecting the head and neck region. Chronic suppurative otitis media refers to chronic inflammation of the middle ear and mastoid cavity associated with a defect in the tympanic membrane. Sinusitis refers to inflammation of the mucous membrane of the paranasal sinuses. Mastoiditis refers to inflammation of the mastoid air cells. Orbital infection refers to infection involving the tissues surrounding the orbit and includes preseptal cellulitis, orbital cellulitis, and orbital abscess. Dental infection refers to infection of the dental pulp. Intracranial complication refers to complications of head and neck infections resulting from spread to deeper structures, such as cerebral venous sinus thrombosis.', NULL, 104351),
