	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_pharery}', 'definition', 'This refers to an inflammatory redness of the phayngeal mucosa', NULL, 104653),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_pharexu}', 'definition', 'This refers to the presence of inflammatory exudative fluid e.g. pus on the pharygeal mucosa', NULL, 104654),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_cyan}', 'definition', 'This refers to a condition of localized tissue damage due to pressure that obstructs blood flow to the skin and subcutaneous tissue.', NULL, 104655),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_cyan}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.', NULL, 104656),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_splenomegaly}', 'definition', 'Defined as an pathological enlargement of the spleen', NULL, 104657),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_tenabd}', 'definition', 'This refers to painful sensation elicited upon touching the abdomen', NULL, 104658),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_feed_npo}', 'definition', 'This refers to clinical orders to indicate that nothing (e.g., medications, food) should be taken by mouth.', NULL, 104659),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_sedated}', 'definition', 'This refers to whether the patient was sedated or paralysed at the time of assessment', NULL, 104660),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_sedated}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.', NULL, 104661),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_focalneuro}', 'definition', 'This refers to impairments of brain function, the nerve or spinal cord that affect a specific region of the body.', NULL, 104662),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_focalneuro}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.', NULL, 104663),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_focalneuro_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of focal neurological deficit. Hemiparesis refers to weakness affecting one side of the body. Cranial nerve palsy refers to loss or impairment of function of one or more cranial nerves. Aphasia refers to impairment of language affecting the ability to speak, understand, read, or write. Visual field deficit refers to partial or complete loss of vision within a portion of the normal visual field. Movement disorder refers to abnormal voluntary or involuntary movements resulting from impaired control of movement.', NULL, 104664),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_focalneuro_type}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) which represents the type of focal neurological deficit', NULL, 104665),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_focalneuro_type_mov}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of movement disorder. Tremor refers to an involuntary, rhythmic, oscillatory movement of a body part. Chorea refers to involuntary, irregular, rapid, non-rhythmic movements that appear to flow randomly from one body part to another. Dystonia refers to sustained or intermittent involuntary muscle contractions causing abnormal, often repetitive movements or postures. Myoclonus refers to sudden, brief, involuntary muscle jerks. Rigidity refers to increased resistance to passive movement that is present throughout the range of motion. Ataxia refers to impaired coordination of voluntary movements.', NULL, 104666),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_focalneuro_type_mov}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) which represents the type of movement disorder', NULL, 104667),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_seizures}', 'definition', 'This refers to condition of involuntary abnormal motor, sensory, autonomic, or behavioural manifestations produced by irregular electrical activity in the brain.', NULL, 104668),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_seizures}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.', NULL, 104669),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_seizures_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the type of seizures. Clinical seizures refer to transient episodes of abnormal motor, sensory, autonomic, or behavioural manifestations. Non-convulsive status epilepticus refers to prolonged seizure activity with altered mental state in the absence of convulsions. EEG-confirmed seizure activity refers to seizure activity demonstrated by electroencephalography, with or without accompanying clinical manifestations. Refractory status epilepticus refers to status epilepticus that persists despite treatment with an adequate dose of a benzodiazepine and a second appropriate antiseizure medication.', NULL, 104670),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_seizures_type}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) which represents the type of seizure disorder', NULL, 104671),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_raiseicp}', 'definition', 'This refers to raised intracranial pressure', NULL, 104672),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_raiseicp}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.', NULL, 104673),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_raiseicp_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to specific clinical signs of raised intracranial pressure experienced by the patient. ', NULL, 104674),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_raiseicp_type}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) which represents the specific clinical signs of raised intracranial pressure experienced by the patient. ', NULL, 104675),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_encephalopathy}', 'definition', 'This refers to a diffuse disruption of brain function and/or structure due to various causes including infection, metabolic disturbances, medication adverse effects, mass effects (e.g., from tumors), and radiation.', NULL, 104676),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_encephalopathy}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate ''Yes'', if the patient experienced this between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.', NULL, 104677),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"LABORATORY RESULTS: Record the value furthest from normal range between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",labs_uric_umoll}', 'definition', 'This refers to the serum uric acid levels', NULL, 104703),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_encephalopathy_type}', 'definition', 'This refers to the specific phenotype of encephalopathy. Delirium is characterized by impairments in attention and awareness (reduced orientation to the environment), as well as other cognitive disturbances (e.g., in memory, language, or perception). Behavioural disturbance refers to abnormal behavioural manuifestation with otherwise intact attention, awareness and cognition. Psychosis refers to an impaired perception of reality characterized by delusions, hallucinations, and/or disorganized thinking.', NULL, 104678),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_encephalopathy_type}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate option(s) which represents the specific phenotype of encephalopathy experienced by the patient. ', NULL, 104679),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"SIGNS: Record the clinical findings observed between 00:00 and 24:00 on the day of assessment",sign_staepil}', 'definition', 'This refers to a condition of localized tissue damage due to pressure that obstructs blood flow to the skin and subcutaneous tissue.', NULL, 104680),
