	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,"LABORATORY RESULTS: Record the value furthest from normal range between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.",lab_csf_gram_result}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropriate response which represents the results of gram stain microscopy on CSF', NULL, 104712),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,IMAGING,imagi_ctbrain_find}', 'definition', 'This refers to the findings of the CT Brain scan. Cerebral oedema is the abnormal accumulation of fluid within the brain parenchyma and on CT, it appears as hypoattenuation with compression and displacement of adjacent structures. Midline shift is a finding described on transverse (axial) slices from CT scans where the midline of the intracranial anatomy is no longer in the midline and is the result of pushing or pulling forces within either side of the intracranial compartment. Hydrocephalus is the abnormal enlargement of the cerebral ventricles due to impaired cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) circulation, absorption, or, overproduction and on CT it shows ventricular dilatation, often with enlarged temporal horns and periventricular low attenuation (transependymal CSF seepage) in acute hydrocephalus. Intracranial haemorrhage is characterised by the extravascular accumulation of blood within different intracranial spaces and on CT, blood appears markedly hyperdense compared to brain parenchyma. Cerebral infarction refers to death of brain tissue due to loss of blood supply. ', NULL, 104713),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,IMAGING,imagi_ctbrain_find}', 'completionGuide', 'Select the most appropiate option which represents the findings on CT Brain scan', NULL, 104714),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,IMAGING,imagi_ctbrain_shift}', 'definition', 'Midline shift is a finding described on transverse (axial) slices from CT scans where the midline of the intracranial anatomy is no longer in the midline and is the result of pushing or pulling forces within either side of the intracranial compartment. Midline shift is measured in millimetres, as the perpendicular distance between a midline structure (usually the septum pellucidum) and a line designated the midline. The midline is assumed to be coplanar with the falx cerebri and is best represented as a line drawn between the anterior and posterior attachments of the falx to the inner table of the skull.', NULL, 104715),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,IMAGING,imagi_ctbrain_shift}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate the degree of midline shift in mm.', NULL, 104716),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,IMAGING,imagi_ctbrain_hemoloc}', 'definition', 'Intracranial haemorrhage is characterised by the extravascular accumulation of blood within different intracranial spaces and on CT, blood appears markedly hyperdense compared to brain parenchyma. C', NULL, 104717),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,IMAGING,imagi_ctbrain_hemoloc}', 'completionGuide', 'Indicate the location of the intracranial haemorrhage', NULL, 104718),
	('2026-08-24 03:43:50.004197+00', '{ARC,daily,IMAGING,imagi_mrib_pattern}', 'definition', 'This refers to the pattern of encephalitis', NULL, 104719),
